    {
      "type": "callout",
      "kind": "tip",
      "title": "What to remember",
      "bullets": [
        "<b>-er</b> and <b>-ir</b> verbs share the same endings, all with <b>í</b>.",
        "<b>yo</b> and <b>él/ella/usted</b> have the same form: <i>hablaba</i>, <i>comía</i>. Use a pronoun or the context when it is not clear.",
        "The only accent on an -ar verb is in <b>nosotros</b>: hablábamos."
      ]
    },
